// Deal or Force - the printing press.
//
// The second monetary lever, and the one the first unlocks: a government that has
// taken the central bank can also have it print. The money is real and arrives at
// once; what it costs is that nobody believes there is a limit any more, and that
// belief does not come back when the press stops.
{
  "Printing money": "Printing money",
  "Have the bank print money and hand it to the treasury, as a share of a year's output. The money is real and arrives at once. What it costs is that nobody believes there is a limit any more - and that belief does not come back when the press stops.": "Have the bank print money and hand it to the treasury, as a share of a year's output. The money is real and arrives at once. What it costs is that nobody believes there is a limit any more - and that belief does not come back when the press stops.",
  "The bank is independent. It will not print for a government that does not own it.": "The bank is independent. It will not print for a government that does not own it.",
  "Nothing is being printed.": "Nothing is being printed.",
  "The press has stopped. It is still costing {0} on prices, because stopping is not the same as never having started.": "The press has stopped. It is still costing {0} on prices, because stopping is not the same as never having started.",
  "{0} a week into the treasury, and {1} on prices - {2} of that is what people remember rather than what you are doing now.": "{0} a week into the treasury, and {1} on prices - {2} of that is what people remember rather than what you are doing now.",
  "Money printed to order": "Money printed to order"
}
